  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The equation of a circle is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> is the radius. If the equation is modified to change the origin other than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, then find out the correct dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> in a new&nbsp;equation :</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>The dimensions of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is given as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mfenced></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
