  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Principle of Homogeneity states that dimensions of each of the terms of a dimensional equation on both sides should be the same. Then,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>For first term,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>T</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>A</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math></p><p>For the second term,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mfrac><mi>t</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>y</mi></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>T</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>B</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mi>B</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
